# Performance and Core Web Vitals

For a shop, speed is revenue and rank. These are limits, not goals. `pnpm check:site` measures the built output and fails on a breach; a change that raises a number must justify it in the PR and update the budget here and in the script in the same commit.

## Targets (mobile, p75 field data; lab Lighthouse mobile as proxy)

| Metric | Limit |
|---|---|
| LCP | ≤ 2.5 s (aim ≤ 2.0 s) |
| INP | ≤ 200 ms |
| CLS | ≤ 0.1 (aim 0) |
| TTFB | ≤ 0.8 s — static HTML from the edge |
| Lighthouse mobile | Performance ≥ 90, SEO 100, Accessibility ≥ 95, Best Practices ≥ 95 |

Measure with `lighthouse_audit` (chrome-devtools MCP) or PageSpeed Insights before calling a page-affecting change done, and after launch use the field data in Search Console.

## Budgets per page (gzip, enforced by `check:site`)

| Asset | Budget |
|---|---|
| JavaScript, summed over everything the page loads (scripts, island components, renderers, their static imports) | ≤ 100 KB |
| CSS (linked + inline) | ≤ 20 KB |
| HTML document | ≤ 25 KB (≤ 70 KB raw; the hero collage and base-path URLs make the home page the largest) |
| Preloaded fonts | ≤ 2 files, ≤ 100 KB total |
| Any single image served | ≤ 200 KB |
| Third-party origins | 0 (no analytics, chat, tag manager, font CDN) until a rule here allows one |

Staff-only routes (`/keystatic`, `/admin`) are exempt from JS budgets but must never be linked from or share chunks with public pages.

## Where each concern lives

- **Rendering and JS:** this file, `check:site` budgets
- **robots.txt, sitemap, canonical host:** generated here (`seo.mdc`); the apex→`www` redirect is Cloudflare config
- **Manual measurement:** GTmetrix, PageSpeed Insights or Lighthouse on the deployed preview. `check:site` guards the build; it does not replace a real-device run

## Rendering

- Static-first: public pages prerender at build. Request-time work only in `src/pages/api/`, `/auth`, `/admin`
- Content the user came for (heading, when/where/free, product name, price) is in the HTML. No client-only render of primary content
- No `client:load`. Use `client:idle` / `client:visible`; a new island must name its reason in the PR. Prefer no island: native `<details>`, `<dialog>`, CSS
- No animation library on public pages. Reveals use CSS transitions + one `IntersectionObserver`. Animate `transform` / `opacity` only; `will-change` only while animating; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- Heavy interactivity (cart dialog, galleries) is lazy: `client:idle` / `client:visible`, never above-the-fold blocking
- No layout reads (`getBoundingClientRect`, `offsetWidth`) during render or scroll handlers

## LCP

- The LCP element (hero image, product image) is in the HTML, not injected by JS
- Exactly one image per page may be eager, and it carries `fetchpriority="high"`. Every other `<img>` is `loading="lazy"` and `decoding="async"`
- Never lazy-load the LCP image; never use a CSS `background-image` for it
- Hero collage: only the first tile is eager (`fetchpriority="high"`); every other tile is lazy, `alt=""`, one `width` (no multi-width srcset, to keep HTML small)

## CLS

- Every `<img>` has `width` and `height` (or `aspect-ratio`). Product grids reserve their space
- Fonts: self-hosted, Latin subset only, `font-display: swap`, the two used weights' variable files preloaded in `<head>` with `crossorigin`. No font CDN
- Nothing is inserted above existing content after load (banners, cart badges reflow-free: reserve their box)
- Dialogs and toasts overlay; they never push content

## Images

- Local images: `src/assets` + `astro:assets` `<Image>`/`<Picture>` (AVIF/WebP, `srcset`, `sizes`). Files in `public/` must already be optimised and ≤ 200 KB
- Shopify CDN images: request the size you display via the `?width=` URL parameter with a `srcset` (see `shopify-image-url`); never ship the original
- Share images: `public/og-default.png` is 1200×630 PNG ≤ 200 KB

## JavaScript hygiene

- No dependency over 10 KB gz in the browser bundle without a PR justification. No `zod`, `lodash`, `moment`, animation libraries in code that ships to public pages — validate by hand or on the server
- Import deep (`no-barrels.mdc`) so tree-shaking works; no side-effect imports
- Public pages must work without JS for reading content and following links. Cart/checkout may need JS

## Caching and delivery

- Hashed assets under `/_astro/` are `immutable`; HTML revalidates. Do not break this with query-string cache busting
- Compression (Brotli) and HTTP/2+ come from Cloudflare; do not inline large assets to "save a request"
- Preconnect only to origins the page really uses (Shopify CDN on shop pages, checkout domain on the cart)

## Review checks

- `pnpm build && pnpm check:site` green; budgets unchanged or the change is justified
- New image has dimensions, correct loading attribute, sane weight
- New dependency: size checked (bundlephobia or `check:site` delta)
- No new third-party origin
